{
  "manufacturer": "Lumel",
  "manufacturer_slug": "lumel",
  "model": "ND31LITE network parameter meter",
  "model_slug": "nd31lite",
  "short_model": "ND31LITE",
  "aliases": [
    "ND31LITE"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (panel network parameter meter)",
  "applies_to": "Lumel ND31LITE panel meter with RS-485 Modbus RTU, per user manual ND31LITE-09.",
  "summary": "The ND31LITE is a 96x96 panel meter for 3- and 1-phase networks with RS-485 Modbus RTU. Its fixed measurement list is offered as floats in several areas; this map uses the 8000 area (two registers per value, high word first), plus comms settings, status words and the 32-bit energy counters from the 4000/4400 areas.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are used as printed: the example frames read 7000 as 0x1B58, 6000 as 0x1770 and 4000 as 0x0FA0. Float registers show the table's 6xxx/8xxx pair in 'documented'; this map uses the 8xxx address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ND31LITE Network parameter meter - User manual",
    "doc_number": "ND31LITE-09",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.lumel.com.pl/resources/Pliki%20do%20pobrania/ND31Lite/ND31LITE_user_manual.pdf",
    "pages": "Example frames pp. 39-40; Table 12 register areas p. 42; Table 13 configuration and Table 16 status/energy pp. 42-53; Table 18 floats pp. 56-62 (PDF pages)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: the area table gives 8000-8970 as bytes 3-2-1-0 and 6000-6970 as 1-0-3-2. The example frames show that 3-2-1-0 means 41 20 00 00 for 10.0 (high word first) and 1-0-3-2 means 00 00 41 20, so the 8000 area is ABCD.",
    "The 7000/7200/7400 areas are a user-programmable group (set in 4200-4259) and are not listed.",
    "Energy counters 4426-4435 follow the manual's formula (high x 65536 + low) / 100.",
    "Left out: 8084 (printed as 'Reactive power averaged (S Demand)' with unit VA, which does not agree), time/date and status floats 8110-8128, the min/max area from 8136, and the alarm/display setup registers.",
    "Frequency (8072) is printed with unit 'f'; it is listed in Hz."
  ],
